{{also|déviant}}
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈdiː.vi.ənt/}}, {{SAMPA|/"di:.vi.@nt/}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Of or pertaining to a [[deviation]]; characterized by deviation from an [[expectation]] or a [[social]] [[standard]].
#: ''At the trial, the extent of his '''deviant''' behavior became clear.''

====Translations====
{{trans-top|of or pertaining to a deviation}}
* Bulgarian: {{t|bg|отклоняващ се}}
* Czech: {{t|cs|deviantní}}, {{t|cs|úchylný|m}}
* Dutch: {{t+|nl|afwijkend}}
* Finnish: {{t+|fi|poikkeava}}
{{trans-mid}}
* French: {{t+|fr|déviant|m}}
* Romanian: {{t-|ro|deviant}}, {{t|ro|deviator|m|n}}
{{trans-bottom}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A person who [[deviate]]s, especially from [[norm]]s of social [[behavior]].
#: ''He was branded as a '''deviant''' and ostracized.''
# A [[thing]], [[phenomenon]], or [[trend]] that deviates from an expectation or [[pattern]].
#: ''As the graph shows, the March sales trend is the '''deviant'''.''

